.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt BN_MOD_EXP_MONT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BN_mod_exp_mont ,
.Nm BN_mod_exp_mont_consttime ,
.Nm BN_mod_exp_mont_consttime_x2
.Nd Montgomery exponentiation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/bn.h
.Ft int
.Fo BN_mod_exp_mont
.Fa "BIGNUM *rr"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *a"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *p"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *m"
.Fa "BN_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "BN_MONT_CTX *in_mont"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo BN_mod_exp_mont_consttime
.Fa "BIGNUM *rr"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *a"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *p"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *m"
.Fa "BN_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "BN_MONT_CTX *in_mont"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo BN_mod_exp_mont_consttime_x2
.Fa "BIGNUM *rr1"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *a1"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *p1"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *m1"
.Fa "BN_MONT_CTX *in_mont1"
.Fa "BIGNUM *rr2"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *a2"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *p2"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *m2"
.Fa "BN_MONT_CTX *in_mont2"
.Fa "BN_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn BN_mod_exp_mont
computes
.Fa a
to the
.Fa p Ns -th
power modulo
.Fa m
.Pf ( Qo Li rr=a^p % m Qc )
using Montgomery multiplication.
.Fa in_mont
is a Montgomery context and can be NULL. In the case
.Fa in_mont
is NULL, it will be initialized within the function, so you can save
time on initialization if you provide it in advance.
.Pp
.Fn BN_mod_exp_mont_consttime
computes
.Fa a
to the
.Fa p Ns -th
power modulo
.Fa m
.Pf ( Qo Li rr=a^p % m Qc )
using Montgomery multiplication.
It is a variant of
.Xr BN_mod_exp_mont 3
that uses fixed windows and the special precomputation memory layout to
limit data-dependency to a minimum to protect secret exponents.
It is called automatically when
.Xr BN_mod_exp_mont 3
is called with parameters
.Fa a ,
.Fa p ,
.Fa m ,
any of which have
.Sy BN_FLG_CONSTTIME
flag.
.Pp
.Fn BN_mod_exp_mont_consttime_x2
computes two independent exponentiations
.Fa a1
to the
.Fa p1 Ns -th
power modulo
.Fa m1
.Pf ( Qo Li rr1=a1^p1 % m1 Qc )
and
.Fa a2
to the
.Fa p2 Ns -th
power modulo
.Fa m2
.Pf ( Qo Li rr2=a2^p2 % m2 Qc )
using Montgomery multiplication.
For some fixed and equal modulus sizes
.Fa m1
and
.Fa m2
it uses optimizations that allow to speedup two exponentiations.
In all other cases the function reduces to two calls of
.Xr BN_mod_exp_mont_consttime 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
For all functions 1 is returned for success, 0 on error.
The error codes can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr BN_mod_exp_mont 3
